new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0e40ca4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ops/logging.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Logging lanes
+
+Observability is split into three lanes. Pick the lane by what the record is
+**for**, not by how severe it feels.
+
+| Lane | How to write | Destination | Retention | Use it for |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | `Log::info()`, `Log::error()`, ... (default `stack`) | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (`daily` driver) | `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` (default 14) | Routine application logs, debug to error. Debugging and forensics. |
+| **Audit** | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` | `storage/logs/audit.log` (`daily` driver) | `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` (default 90), minimum level `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` (default `info`) | A durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail. |
+| **Alert** | `app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send($title, $message, $context)` | Discord incoming webhook (`DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`) | Discord's own history | Actionable production incidents that must page a human. |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+1. **Does a human need to act on this now?** Use the **alert** lane, from the
+   code path that decided the incident is worth paging for (a job that exhausted
+   its retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an
+   entity). Alerts are explicit calls. They are never triggered by a Monolog
+   handler or by every logged error. The incident should still go to the archive.
+2. **Is this a record of an actor changing, or attempting to change, domain
+   state?** Use the **audit** lane. Examples: membership role changes,
+   subscription transitions, login lockouts.
+3. **Anything else** (diagnostics, routine events, errors that nobody must be
+   paged for) goes to the **archive** through the default channel.
+
+Quick check: if you would only read it while debugging, it is archive. If you
+would need to answer "who did this and when" months later, it is audit. If it
+should wake someone up, it is an alert, and it is also archived.
+
+## Rules
+
+- **Discord is not a log channel.** Do not add a `discord` channel to
+  `config/logging.php`, and do not route `Log::` calls to Discord. The
+  notifier is called explicitly.
+- `DiscordOpsAlert` soft-fails. It never throws, and it logs an `error` to the
+  archive when Discord rejects or cannot receive the alert. It is a no-op when
+  `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` is empty, which is the default in local development and
+  tests.
+- Alert text is capped at 1800 characters. Context keys named like
+  `password`, `token`, `secret`, `authorization`, `api_key` or `webhook` are
+  redacted, and so is any `Bearer <credential>` value. Do not rely on that as
+  your only protection: keep secrets out of the context.
+- Never log secrets or PII in any lane (API keys, webhook URLs, tokens,
+  passwords, card data, raw CPF/CNPJ). Audit entries should carry identifiers
+  (`subscription_id`, `actor_id`) and the before/after values of the change, not
+  full personal records.
+- The audit lane is for domain events, not routine debugging. Do not write
+  `debug` entries there. Its minimum level defaults to `info`.
+- Logs are not shipped to any external service. Nothing in this setup sends
+  archive or audit data off the host.
+
+## Examples
+
+```php
+// Audit: a domain transition, with an actor and identifiers only.
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'subscription_id' => $subscription->id,
+    'from' => $from,
+    'to' => $to,
+    'actor_id' => $request->user()->id,
+]);
+
+// Alert: a human must act. Called from the code that detected the incident.
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send('Asaas webhook failing', 'Webhook rejected 3 times', [
+    'queue' => 'asaas-webhooks',
+    'attempts' => 3,
+]);
+```
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels behind the default `stack`. `daily` is the archive. The test environment pins it to `daily` in `phpunit.xml`. |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention in days. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level written to the audit lane. |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention in days. |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | empty (disabled) | Discord incoming webhook for `DiscordOpsAlert`. Treat it as a secret. |
+
+Tests for the channels and the notifier live in `tests/Feature/Ops/`.
